      "content": "Swollen batteries, a serious hazard, must be handled with extreme caution. Do not try to squeeze or puncture it, as this can cause a fire or explosion, and you'll want to keep it away from any flammable materials. The standard procedure is to carefully remove the battery from the device, if possible, and then immediately isolate it. You must treat it as hazardous waste, and most electronics recycling centers or local waste management facilities have specific protocols for lithium-ion batteries.",
